//@@ ch16-eventual-consistency
CH({slug:'ch16-eventual-consistency',n:'16',part:'Part IV · Running them',sub:'Why two services can disagree for a while, and how to live with it.',end:'Given the same events, everyone ends up in the same place.',scenes:[
QT('It’s really about convergence','Once every message is delivered, all replicas *agree.*','The person who coined “eventual consistency” later said it should have been “eventual convergence”.'),
PT('Each consumer lives in a time bubble',[['Consumer lag','One service is behind another in consuming or storing.','amber'],['Producer lag','A producer’s state is current, but it isn’t writing to the stream.','red'],['Usually harmless','Services sit at the head of their streams, unless new or reset.','green']],['A consumer can tell you what it has, not what it hasn’t seen yet.','The real trouble: one context <b>querying another directly</b>.']),
VS('Example: assigning drivers to trucks','Two streams, one lagging',['The truck service is 7 hours behind','Drivers are assigned to trucks that already left','Each service is right, in its own bubble'],'One atomic event',['Driver and truck in the same event','They line up exactly in time','Only when the domain allows it'],['If two facts must line up exactly, <b>put them in the same event</b>.']),
VS('When the streams themselves disagree','Wait',['Hold the join open','Perhaps emit a partial result','Update it when the data arrives'],'Give up',['After a deadline','Emit without the missing side','Giving up is final'],['Even an infinitely fast consumer can’t join what hasn’t been produced.'],'or','blue','amber'),
PT('Strategies for living with it',[['Prefer state events','Easier to apply identically than deltas.'],['Expose it in the response','Like a “please wait to confirm” spinner, between servers.'],['Don’t query across contexts','Consume the stream and keep your own copy.'],['Join facts in one event','When they must agree in time.']]),
RC('16',[['Convergence','Same events, same end state.'],['Time bubbles','Each consumer has its own “now”.'],['Lag','Consumer-side or producer-side.'],['Missing data','Wait, or give up.'],['Design for it','State events and atomic facts.']])
]});
